    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey can u give me a quick breakdown of the stages for a standard CI/CD pipeline? specifically i need the stages for code commit, automated testing, staging, and production deployment. also just include what kind of gates/checks should be at each stage so we can make sure nothing breaks. thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A standard CI/CD pipeline typically includes the following stages:\n\n1. **Source Branch Check**: Automated check of the source branch to ensure code changes are up-to-date and haven't been merged with main codebase (by default).\n2. **Automated Testing**: Run automated unit tests, integration tests, and UI tests to validate code quality.\n3. **Code Review**: Initial code review by a human reviewer to catch potential issues that automated tests may have missed.\n4. **Staging**: Validate deployable code in a staging environment to ensure it works as expected before releasing to production.\n5. **Production Deployment**: Deploy validated code to production if all previous stages pass.\n\nGates/checks at each stage:\n- Source Branch Check: Branch branch is up-to-date and hasn't been merged.\n- Automated Testing: Tests pass.\n- Code Review: Code is clean, follows best practices, and doesn't introduce new bugs.\n- Staging: Deployment works as expected, and validation checks pass.\n- Production Deployment: Prior stages passed.",
      "source": "target",
